  "research_id": "sec-tokenized-nms-stock-innovation-exemption",
  "title": "SEC Tokenized NMS Stock Innovation Exemption — 2026 Order",
  "question": "What did the SEC's effective Tokenized NMS Stock Innovation Exemption authorize, and which venue, issuer, record, liquidity, custody, clearing, settlement and token-selection gates remain?",
  "bluf": "Release 34-106402 is an effective, temporary Commission order through September 17, 2031. It creates a conditional exchange-definition exemption for a Tokenized Securities Venue operating permissioned AMM pools on public, permissionless DLT and a dealer-definition exemption for qualifying own-account liquidity providers. A pool may pair Tokenized NMS Stock with another such stock, any non-security crypto asset or a tokenized money market fund. No TSV may operate until its complete 30-day public-notice clock has run, and the order does not itself authorize issuance, transfer agency, custody, clearing, bank cash, legal settlement finality or any named token, chain or company.",
